+      {/* EVENT TOKEN */}
+      <section className="rsp-burn-section" id="event-token">
+        <div className="rsp-burn-inner">
+          <div>
+            <div className="rsp-burn-label">Tier 6 — New Token Type</div>
+            <div className="rsp-burn-quote">
+              Proof that coordination happened.{' '}
+              <em>Proof that identity was burned.</em>
+            </div>
+            <p className="rsp-burn-body">
+              RSP Event Tokens are non-identifiable on-chain records of validated coordination events.
+              Each token is minted at the moment a behaviour is translated into a weighted signal — after
+              the validation delay clears and the event is committed to node state. The source identity
+              is cryptographically destroyed at or before minting. The token is the proof the event
+              occurred, not who caused it.
+            </p>
+            <p className="rsp-burn-body" style={{ marginTop: 16 }}>
+              Supply is unbounded — one token per validated coordination event across all nodes.
+              Tokens are aggregatable into node health proofs and composable across circles and systems.
